# web/
This directory contains the TypeScript formatting and rendering layer for financial reports. `format.ts` supplies shared helpers for currency, month labels, and text alignment, while `render.ts` defines the report data shape and turns that data into either aligned plain text or HTML output.

## format.ts
`format.ts` centralizes presentation details used by the report renderer. `formatCents` treats monetary values as integer cents and produces signed, comma-grouped currency with exactly two decimal places; `formatMonth` turns `YYYY-MM` keys into labels such as `Jan 2024`; and `pad` creates fixed-width, optionally right-aligned text for tabular output.

## format.ts, render.ts
`render.ts` is the main report-facing module: it describes monthly totals and ranked category data, then consumes the helpers from `format.ts` to produce the final representations. `renderText` builds aligned headings, monthly rows, and a top-categories section, while `renderHtml` builds a monthly table and category list, marking negative net values with `neg` and all others with `pos`. The HTML renderer inserts category text without escaping, so its callers must provide safe data.
